{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact shared head 870ee66f89f53b5daa12a37d7127eab3001755be, primary27c39eb7 and companions562e1d4a/cfd97a50, under current parent review requestf61f4b29 and my promisec59a6fdf. The two commits carry the correct distinct Rests-On requests: b6489d7b for filing-progress request3a4a54e4 (Claude promisea49e9916), and 870ee66f for worker-timeout childc2659dea (Claude promise60cfc738). I reviewed the complete shared head and all three artifacts; the worker correction also has its own independent verdict on review requestff05325c.\n\nArchitecture. The affected layer is layer7 CLI/performance-command test coverage. cmd/gs/main.go and cmd/gitseq-perf/main.go are byte-identical to current main c0108be8. No production, kernel, profile, projection, admission or public contract changes; the architecture page therefore needs no update. Filing tests now ignore only empty lines and the exact legitimate slow-audit notice, while malformed/local-absent/foreign/retired warnings, ordering before refusal/signing, exit status and signed-basis/state checks remain enforced. Deterministic progress injection execs the real binary with positional arguments; no production delay hook is introduced. The shared worker test now distinguishes timeout termination from ordinary exit7 and preserves pre-start deadline refusal and pipe lifetime.\n\nSecurity. The exact-line filter cannot discard an unrelated warning just because the notice is present. The wrapper passes the binary, repository and command arguments as shell positional parameters with quoted exec \"$@\", rather than generating shell code from paths. New controls prove valid progress remains quiet about the filing and a malformed-basis warning survives. Neither half alters signing, keys, runtime subprocess behavior or authority. No unresolved security defect found; ordinary assigned request authority governs these two test corrections, not the special authority-bearing request-chain alternative.\n\nSimplification. One shared notice constant and one line filter replace two overly broad empty-stderr assumptions. The fixture helper reuses the ordinary command/capture path, and the worker's single predicate is exercised by both successful enforcement and rejected ordinary exits. These are small test-only helpers serving distinct assertions; no further simplification is needed without losing a condition.\n\nValidation and provenance. I verified the two filing files at870ee66f are byte-identical to the previously examined e7f8e6ff and reread their complete diff against main. My earlier four targeted filing tests passed in10.109s on that identical source; that is carried evidence, not a fresh full-package run. All three parent evidence attachments are byte-identical to the earlier fully read packet; the author reports the unchanged filing commit's targeted12 subtests, full cmd/gs package344.839s, vet/build and both omission controls. At this new shared head my fresh full worker package -race passes5.566s, and the independent immediate-exit7 overlay fails both timeout fixtures as required in0.678s. I also read the new worker gates/mutants in full. git diff --check passes, both production main.go files equal main, and origin holds the exact reviewed branch head. I did not rerun the entire module or claim fresh filing/full-module results.\n\nThe citation set deliberately includes both reporting artifacts and all three exact changed paths. Under the documented shared review-binding resolver, both implementation commitments therefore join this approval even though the primary is the filing artifact. A sealed merge on this approval should close both; do not add a duplicate explicit child report if the receipt already names it. Both separately requested review verdicts must be ratified, and the explicit S1-first landing priority remains a gate. This approval is for this exact head only; any correction requires a new artifact packet and fresh review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d26